[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Step 1: Use the fact that $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m This is a key geometric condition. Let’s denote the triangle in standard triangle notation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ A $ is a vertex
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ B $ and $ C $ are the other two vertices
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ O $ is the circumcenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ I $ is the incenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m We are told that $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $. This implies that the vector from $ I $ to $ A $ is perpendicular to the vector from $ O $ to $ I $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m This is a very special condition that will help us find relations between the sides and angles of the triangle.
