[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Step 3: Use the condition $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m This is a special geometric condition that can be used to derive a relation between the sides and angles of the triangle.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s recall that in a triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - The **distance between the incenter and circumcenter** is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m   $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m   IO^2 = R(R - 2r)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m   $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m IO^2 = 13(13 - 2 \cdot 6) = 13(13 - 12) = 13 \cdot 1 = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m IO = \sqrt{13}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Now, we are told that $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $, so the triangle $ \triangle IAO $ is a right triangle with right angle at $ I $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So in $ \triangle IAO $, we have:
