[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ IO $ is the other leg
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ AO $ is the hypotenuse
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m AO^2 = IA^2 + IO^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m We also know that the **distance from the circumcenter $ O $ to vertex $ A $** is the **circumradius** $ R = 13 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m AO = R = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 13^2 = IA^2 + IO^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \Rightarrow 169 = IA^2 + 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \Rightarrow IA^2 = 156
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \Rightarrow IA = \sqrt{156} = 2\sqrt{39}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
