[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Step 1: Set up equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - Time at speed $ s $: $ T_1 = 4 $ hours (including $ t $ minutes in the shop)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - Time at speed $ s + 2 $: $ T_2 = 2 $ hours 24 minutes = $ 2 + \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s convert all times to hours for consistency:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ T_1 = 4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $ T_2 = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s denote the time spent walking (excluding the coffee shop) as $ t_w $, and the time spent in the coffee shop as $ t $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So, the total time for each walk is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s $: $ t_w + t = 4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s + 2 $: $ t_w + t = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m But we also know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - Distance = speed × time
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - Distance is always 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 1. $ 9 = s \cdot t_w $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 2. $ 9 = (s + 2) \cdot t_w $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m We now have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m s \cdot t_w = 9 \quad \text{(1)}
