[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Correct Interpretation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s re-read the problem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m > "When she walks at a constant speed of $ s $ kilometers per hour, the walk takes her 4 hours, including $ t $ minutes spent in the coffee shop. When she walks $ s + 2 $ kilometers per hour, the walk takes her 2 hours and 24 minutes, including $ t $ minutes spent in the coffee shop."
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So the **total time** (including the coffee shop) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s $: 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s + 2 $: 2 hours 24 minutes = 2.4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So the **time spent walking** (excluding the coffee shop) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s $: $ 4 - t/60 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - At speed $ s + 2 $: $ 2.4 - t/60 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Then:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \text{Distance} = \text{speed} \times \text{time walking}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 1. $ 9 = s \cdot (4 - \frac{t}{60}) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 2. $ 9 = (s + 2) \cdot (2.4 - \frac{t}{60}) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Now we have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m s \left(4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m (s + 2)\left(2.4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s solve these equations.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Step 2: Solve the system of equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m From (1):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m s \left(4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9 \Rightarrow s = \frac{9}{4 - \frac{t}{60}} = \frac{9}{\frac{240 - t}{60}} = \frac{9 \cdot 60}{240 - t} = \frac{540}{240 - t} \quad \text{(A)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m From (2):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m (s + 2)\left(2.4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Substitute $ s = \frac{540}{240 - t} $ into this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \left(\frac{540}{240 - t} + 2\right)\left(2.4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Simplify the first term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{540}{240 - t} + 2 = \frac{540 + 2(240 - t)}{240 - t} = \frac{540 + 480 - 2t}{240 - t} = \frac{1080 - 2t}{240 - t}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So now the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{1080 - 2t}{240 - t} \cdot \left(2.4 - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Convert 2.4 to a fraction:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 2.4 = \frac{144}{60} = \frac{12}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{1080 - 2t}{240 - t} \cdot \left(\frac{12}{5} - \frac{t}{60}\right) = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Find a common denominator for the terms in the second factor:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{12}{5} - \frac{t}{60} = \frac{144 - t}{60}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{1080 - 2t}{240 - t} \cdot \frac{144 - t}{60} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Multiply both sides by 60:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \frac{(1080 - 2t)(144 - t)}{240 - t} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Now multiply both sides by $ 240 - t $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m (1080 - 2t)(144 - t) = 540(240 - t)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Expand both sides:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Left side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
