[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Given that $\overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI}$, this means the vector $\vec{IA}$ is perpendicular to the vector $\vec{OI}$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So, the dot product of $\vec{IA}$ and $\vec{OI}$ is zero:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \vec{IA} \cdot \vec{OI} = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $O = (0, 0)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $I = (x, y)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m - $A = (a, b)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Then:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \vec{IA} = (a - x, b - y), \quad \vec{OI} = (x, y)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Their dot product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m (a - x)x + (b - y)y = 0 \Rightarrow ax - x^2 + by - y^2 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ax + by = x^2 + y^2 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m ### Step 3: Use the fact that $O$ is the circumcenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m The circumradius $R = 13$, so the distance from $O$ to any vertex is 13:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m OA = OB = OC = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
