[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m x + \frac{26}{x} + \frac{26}{y} + \ldots + \frac{26}{z} = 18
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m But this is too complex.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m Instead, we can use the fact that the polygon is non-convex, and that the side $ A_1A_{11} = 2 $ is the only one not part of the product.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So the sum of the other 9 sides is 18, and the answer is $ A_1A_2 + 2 $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m So the answer is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m \boxed{A_1A_2 + 2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13888)[0m But we need
